## Declaring a dataset

Declare every dataset in the front matter above. `uv run build.py check` validates the
declarations.

| Field | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `id` | a short identifier, used by notebooks as `dataset:<id>` |
| `tier` | `public`, `licensed`, `confidential` (identifiable people), or `restricted` (a contract or ethics board forbids sharing) |
| `license` | an SPDX identifier, a license name, or `unknown` |
| `raw` | `true` for raw data, which is never modified |
| `paths` | repository paths where the data lives or would be placed, such as `data/raw/survey/` |
| `location` | where the data is kept outside the repository |
| `version` | a version or access date, recorded with every output that uses the dataset |

Tier and license are declared separately. Where they impose different rules on storage,
processing, or release, the most restrictive one applies. Files at the paths of raw datasets, and
of datasets whose tier is not public, must not be committed; the checks and the pre-commit hook
refuse them. Small approved derived data may be committed. Large data belongs in the configured
store. Data is stored as parquet.

## What this project accepts

This project accepts only public, synthetic, or owner-approved derived data. Confidential and
restricted data do not enter it. The guidance below is for work that happens upstream of this
project. The template does not provide or verify it.

- **Isolation.** Keeping data outside the working tree, or processing it outside an agent session,
  does not stop an agent that runs with the same file permissions from reading it. Effective
  isolation needs a separately provisioned environment with no access to the sensitive data.
  Agent read-deny settings are an extra layer, never a guarantee.
- **De-identification.**
  - Remove direct identifiers.
  - Replace IDs with keyed hashes whose key lives outside the repository.
  - Coarsen quasi-identifiers: age bands, broader geography, shifted or coarsened dates.
  - Scrub names and contact details from free text with a PII detector run locally, and spot-check
    the result by hand.
  - Check small cells before release.
  - Keep any re-identification key separate from the data.
- **Models.** Send sensitive data only to approved endpoints: an institutional gateway with
  no-retention terms, or a local model.
- **Model-based measurements.** Outputs of LLM or other model-based measurement are produced by
  scripts and stored as data of record with the model, prompt, and date. The build never
  regenerates them; rerunning creates a new dataset version.
- **Openness.** Decide for each dataset what can be shared:
  - the raw data;
  - the derived data;
  - identifiers only, so others can rebuild it under their own license;
  - synthetic data plus access instructions;
  - an availability statement only.

